<doxygen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="compound.xsd" version="1.9.1" xml:lang="en-US">
  <compounddef id="Reallocate-example" kind="example">
    <compoundname>Reallocate</compoundname>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Reallocate aligned memory from system heap. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Reallocate aligned memory from system heap<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ptr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to existing aligned allocation </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>old_bytes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Size of existing allocation in bytes </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>new_bytes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Desired new size in bytes </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>alignment</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Required alignment in bytes (must be power of 2) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>zeroed</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If true, zero-initialize new bytes when growing (default: false) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Expected&lt;void*&gt; containing pointer to reallocated aligned memory or error</para>
</simplesect>
Like realloc(), but maintains the specified alignment. The returned pointer is guaranteed to be aligned to the specified boundary.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Never</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>throws</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>with new aligned pointer on success </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>with NullPointerError if ptr is null </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>with InvalidArgError if new_bytes is 0 </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>with ReallocFailError if new allocation fails</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
cache-aligned buffer <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">cslt::HeapAllocator<sp/>allocator;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Initial<sp/>64-byte<sp/>aligned<sp/>allocation</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">auto<sp/>result1<sp/>=<sp/>allocator.alloc_aligned(512,<sp/>64,<sp/>false);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">void*<sp/>ptr<sp/>=<sp/>result1.value();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Grow<sp/>while<sp/>maintaining<sp/>64-byte<sp/>alignment</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">auto<sp/>result2<sp/>=<sp/>allocator.realloc_aligned(ptr,<sp/>512,<sp/>1024,<sp/>64,<sp/>false);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">if<sp/>(result2.hasValue())<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>void*<sp/>new_ptr<sp/>=<sp/>result2.value();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>Verify<sp/>alignment<sp/>maintained</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>assert(reinterpret_cast&lt;uintptr_t&gt;(new_ptr)<sp/>%<sp/>64<sp/>==<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>allocator.return_element(new_ptr,<sp/>1024,<sp/>64);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>The alignment parameter must match the alignment used in the original allocation.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>realloc() For non-aligned reallocation </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>alloc_aligned() For initial aligned allocation <programlisting filename="Reallocate"></programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
